  "notes": "Compatible with Arista Networks QSFP-100G-LR4; TAA compliant; DOM supported. Average launch power min (-4.3 dBm) and average receive power min (-10.6 dBm) per lane are informative per notes. Receive sensitivity -8.6 dBm (OMA per lane); stressed receiver sensitivity (OMA) -6.8 dBm measured with conformance test signal at TP3 for BER = 10^-12. Stressed sensitivity test conditions include VECP 1.8 dB, J2 0.3 UI, J9 0.47 UI (not receiver characteristics). Transmitter and dispersion penalty (TDP) each lane max 2.2 dB. Optical Modulation Amplitude (OMA) per lane Tx -1.3 to 4.5 dBm; Rx OMA max 4.5 dBm. Difference in launch power between any two lanes (OMA) max 5 dB. Launch power in OMA minus TDP each lane min -2.3 dBm. Average launch power of OFF transmitter per lane max -30 dBm. Relative Intensity Noise max -130 dB/Hz. Optical Return Loss min -26 dB. Receiver damage threshold per lane min 5.5 dBm. Data rate variation -100 to +100 ppm. Storage temperature -40 to 85 °C. Note 2 hit ratio 5x10^-5.",
